{#
  The two channels, on the record they read from.
#}
<div class="ccr-actions">
  {% if stale_decks %}
    <div class="ccr-alert ccr-alert--stale">
      <strong>{{ stale_decks }}</strong> deck{{ stale_decks == 1 ? '' : 's' }} generated from this record
      {{ stale_decks == 1 ? 'is' : 'are' }} out of date.
      <a href="/admin/content/decks">Open My decks</a>
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  {#
    Two lists, because they are two different kinds of problem. A blocking issue
    stops the deck being made at all — too many pillars for this template, a
    required field left empty, a font the renderer cannot measure. The rest is
    text that will not fit its box: worth fixing, but the deck still comes out.

    Both are shown. Showing only the blocking one meant a marketer fixed the
    pillar count, pressed Generate again, and only then met "49 characters,
    limit is 36" — one problem per attempt, which is the slowest possible way
    to find out what is wrong.
  #}
  {% set blocked = issues|filter(i => i.blocking) %}
  {% set fit = issues|filter(i => not i.blocking) %}

  {% if blocked %}
    <div class="ccr-alert ccr-alert--blocked">
      <strong>No deck can be made from this record{{ blocked|length > 1 ? ' yet' : '' }}:</strong>
      <ul>
        {% for issue in blocked %}
          <li>{{ issue.message }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if fit %}
    <div class="ccr-alert ccr-alert--fit">
      <strong>This will not fit the slide:</strong>
      <ul>
        {% for issue in fit %}
          <li>{{ issue.label }} — {{ issue.message }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="ccr-actions__buttons">
    {% for action in actions %}
      <a href="{{ action.url }}" class="ccr-button{{ action.primary ? ' ccr-button--primary' : '' }}" title="{{ action.hint }}">
        {{ action.title }}
      </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
